    "result_text": "The build passes with all tests green. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded an optional `registrationDate` to the owner that defaults to the server's current date on create and is returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `registrationDate` property (`type: string`, `format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. The generator maps this to a `LocalDate` on both `OwnerFieldsDto` (input) and `OwnerDto` (output), and Jackson serializes `LocalDate` as `YYYY-MM-DD`. It's not in the `required` list, so it's optional on create.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a persisted `LocalDate registrationDate` field (`registration_date` column) with getter/setter, alongside the existing owner fields.\n\n3. **DB schemas** \u2014 Added a `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table in all four schemas (hsqldb \u2014 used by tests, plus h2/mysql/postgres for consistency).\n\n4. **`DefaultRegistrationDate.java`** (new function) \u2014 A single-responsibility pipeline step that, reading the built `Owner` via `@Val`, stamps `LocalDate.now()` only when no date was supplied, preserving a supplied one.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 Wired the new step in between `build` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\nThe existing MapStruct mapper maps `registrationDate` by name in both directions with no change needed, and the PUT path (which sets fields explicitly) is untouched. Both new acceptance tests (`coreDefaultsToToday`, `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate`) and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
